🎗️ 27.7 Why Do We Need synchronized?

🔴 Both Producer and Consumer access the same shared queue.

👉 Without synchronization:

Producer
    ↓
buffer.offer()

Consumer
    ↓
buffer.poll()

🔴 Both threads could access the shared queue simultaneously.
🔴 This can result in a race condition.

Therefore:

public synchronized void produce(...)
and
public synchronized Object consume()

are used.

🔴 Both methods synchronize on the same SharedBuffer object's monitor.

 SharedBuffer
      ↓
   Monitor
   ↙      ↘
Producer   Consumer

🎗️ 27.8 Why wait()?

👉 Suppose:

Capacity = 5
Buffer = [1,2,3,4,5]

🔴 The Producer wants to add 6.
🔴 But the buffer is full.
🔴 It should not continuously check:

while(buffer.size() == capacity) {

}

🔴 This is busy waiting and wastes CPU.

👉 Instead: wait();
When a thread calls wait():

Thread
   ↓
WAITING
   ↓
Releases Monitor
   ↓
Another Thread can acquire Monitor

🎗️ 27.9 Why while Instead of if?

👉 Wrong
if(buffer.size() == capacity) {
    wait();
}

👉 Correct
while(buffer.size() == capacity) {
    wait();
}

👉 Similarly for Consumer:

while(buffer.isEmpty()) {
    wait();
}

Why?

The condition must be checked again after the thread wakes up.

👉 Reasons include:
🔴 Spurious wakeups
🔴 Multiple Producers,Multiple Consumers,Another thread changing the buffer state before the awakened thread reacquires the monitor

Therefore:

wait()
  ↓
Wake Up
  ↓
Re-check Condition
  ↓
Can I proceed?
  ↓
Yes → Continue
No  → wait() again

🎗️ 27.10 Why notifyAll()?

👉 After Producer inserts an item:

buffer.offer(itemProduced);
notifyAll();

🔴 The Consumer may be waiting because the buffer was empty.

👉 Similarly, after Consumer removes an item:

buffer.poll();
notifyAll();

🔴 The Producer may be waiting because the buffer was full.

Therefore:

Producer adds item
       ↓
Buffer state changes
       ↓
notifyAll()
       ↓
Waiting threads wake

And:

Consumer removes item
       ↓
Buffer state changes
       ↓
notifyAll()
       ↓
Waiting threads wake

🎗️ 27.11 Why notifyAll() Instead of notify()?

👉 With multiple Producers and Consumers:

Producer-1
Producer-2
Consumer-1
Consumer-2

🔴 notify() wakes only one waiting thread.
🔴 That thread may not be the appropriate one to proceed.
🔴 notifyAll() wakes all waiting threads, and each thread re-checks its condition.

notifyAll()
     ↓
All waiting threads wake
     ↓
Each checks its condition
     ↓
Correct thread proceeds

