🎗️ 27.22 Why Same SharedBuffer Object?

👉 This is extremely important.
Correct:

SharedBuffer sharedBuffer = new SharedBuffer(5);

Thread consumerThread = new Consumer(sharedBuffer);
Thread producerThread = new Producer(sharedBuffer);

🔴 Both threads use:
     SharedBuffer
          ↓
       Queue
       ↙   ↘
Producer   Consumer

🔴 If we created separate objects:

Producer → Buffer-1
Consumer → Buffer-2

🔴 They would not share the same queue.
🔴 Therefore, communication would fail.

