🎗️ 27.27 Important Observation

👉 The output order is not guaranteed between Producer and Consumer because thread scheduling is controlled by the JVM/OS.

For example:

Producer produces 1
Consumer consumes 1
Producer produces 2
Producer produces 3
Consumer consumes 2
...

or:

Consumer waits
Producer produces 1
Producer produces 2
Consumer consumes 1
...

Both are valid as long as:

✔ No item is consumed before being produced
✔ Buffer never exceeds capacity
✔ Consumer waits when buffer is empty
✔ Producer waits when buffer is full


